  "native_complete_decoded0": {
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "Lp ℝ 2 μ is the Hilbert space of real-valued square-integrable classes for the stated measure;→L[ℝ] means bounded real-linear operators. IsPositive means symmetric with nonnegative quadratic form. Commute A B means A*B=B*A;operator multiplication is composition.",
      "All witnesses following existential quantifiers are concluded data,not public assumptions. Exact initial caller binders delimit the input conditions.",
      "Measure.tilted denotes normalized exponential tilting. The Gaussian product pushforward, reflected law and every-state normalized kernel are produced, with per-observable AE conditional actions.",
      "Lp exponent2 is the complete real Hilbert space of square-integrable almost-everywhere classes. lpMeas is the closed measurable subspace for the displayed comap sigma algebra. condExpL2 is conditional expectation. The measurable-space Fact is derived internally.",
      "Subtype maps are inclusions; the pullback isometric equivalence is produced. Isometric conjugation sends C to e C e.symm. Multiplication of bounded endomorphisms is composition; IsPositive means selfadjoint with nonnegative quadratic form.",
      "The constant q, integral pairing, exact centered kernel HP0, positive restricted root, unit and two-sided bounded inverse are produced. Their inherited complete Hilbert structures are internal, not premises.",
      "Hperp is the kernel of the displayed conditional-expectation operator P, not merely the globally zero-mean space. B0 and V0 are bounded real maps between the exact displayed subspaces. adjoint is the Hilbert adjoint. V0.adjoint composed V0=I asserts an isometry into Hperp; no onto or reverse-product identity is concluded.",
      "The displayed statement is the exact definitional expansion of the compiled theorem type,whose private Prop definition has this literal complete value. The original caller binders are unchanged. A Prop-valued definition records a proposition and supplies no proof or mathematical premise. Whole-module source review receives the actual private definition and theorem header separately.",
      "R is a produced bounded map from the joint Hilbert space to ker P;coercion back to the joint space is g-Pg. The ambient Hilbert adjoint has all joint L² observables as domain;its intrinsic block action is recovered by the displayed R. The last centered-input implication quantifies every joint f with zero Bochner integral;the conditional mean and corrector are internally constructed in the same centered macroscopic subspace.",
      "A0 is the internally produced restriction to the exact centered subspace HP0;the SAME Inv is both-sided inverse of the SAME Γ0. All old global-observable conclusions persist. A private literal Prop definition only stages the complete original proposition and gives no proof or premise.",
      "D is the displayed residual compression of the same produced isometric involution. The adjoint-composition equality is asserted on the whole displayed conditional-complement domain, not only the range of the produced isometry.",
      "For each globally mean-zero input f, the output g is exactly U(P f-(f-P f)). Its macro vector is the conditional-expectation component identified by the displayed inclusion; its second vector is V0.adjoint(R g). These output components are not defined by the asserted right-hand sides. The zero output mean is a conclusion, not an input premise."
    ],
